                <pb facs="0935" n="823" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg823"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 891.001.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Russell.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-09-23"><hi rendition="#italic">September 23,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The President has cabled to the Shah his sympathy upon the death of the Regent,
                    and the Secretary of State has cabled similarly to the <pb facs="0936" n="824"
                        xml:id="pg824"/> minister for foreign affairs. If you have not already done
                    so, you will convey to the minister for foreign affairs proper expression of
                    sympathy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
